<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">The Ballad of Mulan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">believed composed under the Northern Wei (386–<a href="/years/535">535 CE</a>); first written down in the 6th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a> · Also known as 木蘭詩, Mùlán shī</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ballad of Mulan is the first known written record of Mulan, the legendary heroine who took her aged father's place in the army by disguising herself as a man. It is a folk song believed to have been composed during the Northern Wei regime (386–535 CE).</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>The Ballad of Mulan</b> is the first known written record of Mulan, the legendary heroine who took her aged father's place in the army by disguising herself as a man.</blockquote><a href="/songs/ballad-of-mulan">The Ballad of Mulan</a></li></ul></section>
